983
00:57:42,000 --> 00:57:45,867
可悲的是，他忙着跟萨克斯代尔队比赛，根本没听进去。
Sadly, he was too busy racing
Team Saxondale to listen.

984
00:57:46,567 --> 00:57:48,167
我抓到他了！
And I've got him!

985
00:57:48,200 --> 00:57:50,433
在斯托（其实是科普斯）里把他逼到内线。
Took him
on the inside at Stowe.
I mean, Copse.

986
00:57:50,467 --> 00:57:52,533
杰里米，是理查德。我知道你正忙。
Jeremy, it's Richard.
I know you're busy.

987
00:57:52,567 --> 00:57:55,033
说说轮胎情况吧，感觉还行吗？
Tell us about the tyres.
Do they feel okay?

988
00:57:56,967 --> 00:57:59,467
我把萨克斯代尔气得要命。
I've got Saxondale
up my trumpet.

989
00:57:59,500 --> 00:58:00,800
我……哦，掉挡了！
I've got... Oh, missed a gear!

990
00:58:06,167 --> 00:58:07,633
哇！天啊！
Whoa! God!

991
00:58:09,000 --> 00:58:11,933
HAMMOND: 哈蒙德：杰里米把轮胎毁了。
HAMMOND: Jeremy
had destroyed the tyres.

992
00:58:11,967 --> 00:58:15,200
刚收到史蒂夫的消息。我们有轮胎专家在维修区。
Just heard from Steve.
We have our tyre expert
in the pit lane.

993
00:58:15,233 --> 00:58:20,233
他检查了其他轮胎，说你的只能再撑大约三分钟。
He's looked at the other tyres
and says yours will last
about another three minutes.

994
00:58:20,267 --> 00:58:22,367
我们必须让他进来。
We had to get him in.

995
00:58:22,400 --> 00:58:26,233
萨克斯代尔在我们换胎期间还能跑满五圈。
Saxondale would rack up
five laps while our tyres
were changed.

996
00:58:28,167 --> 00:58:31,533
但换上新胎后，杰里米现在可以全力加速。
But on fresh rubber,
Jeremy could now
get the hammer down.

997
00:58:31,567 --> 00:58:33,833
[引擎轰鸣]
[ENGINES ROARING]

998
00:58:44,600 --> 00:58:47,933
圈速更新。萨克斯代尔回应，2分24秒。
Lap update.
Saxondale responding, 2.24.

999
00:58:47,967 --> 00:58:50,500
CLARKSON: 克拉克森：把你们的念珠擦亮吧，伙计们。
CLARKSON: Get rubbing
your rosaries, boys.

1000
00:58:50,533 --> 00:58:52,733
哇，天啊！
Whoa, God!

1001
00:58:52,767 --> 00:58:56,667
我刚想在弯道内侧抢车，结果弄得一团糟。
I just tried to take the track
on the inside of the corner
and it went badly wrong.

1002
00:58:56,700 --> 00:59:01,633
如果你在比赛最后半小时掉队，根本找不到救援，
If you fall off in the last
half hour of the race,
there's no recovery service,

1003
00:59:01,667 --> 00:59:03,267
也就是说，你的比赛完蛋了。
which mean that's the end
of your race.

1004
00:59:08,800 --> 00:59:10,867
CLARKSON: 好在，咱们运气还行。
CLARKSON: Happily,
we got some luck.

1005
00:59:10,900 --> 00:59:13,000
Saxondale 那帮子出现了点儿麻烦，
The Saxondale team
had hit problems,

1006
00:59:13,033 --> 00:59:16,767
所以我只能把车小心翼翼地抱回去。
so now all I had to do
was nurse the car home.

1007
00:59:18,233 --> 00:59:20,700
加油，车啊，别掉链子。
Come on, car. Please make it.

1008
00:59:26,167 --> 00:59:30,000
这可是《Top Gear》历来最牛的伙伴之一。
This has been
one of the best Top Gear
companions of the lot.

1009
00:59:30,033 --> 00:59:34,033
一辆烂车，十天打造成赛车。
A wreck-mobile,
transformed in 10 days
into a racer.

1010
00:59:37,167 --> 00:59:38,700
还有十五分钟。
Fifteen minutes to go.

1011
00:59:40,633 --> 00:59:44,200
现在有点儿马虎了，失误频出。
Starting to get
a bit sloppy now.
We're getting a few mistakes.

1012
00:59:46,167 --> 00:59:48,733
只剩五分钟，第一次，
Five minutes to go
and for the first time,

1013
00:59:48,767 --> 00:59:51,767
我感觉这只尿渍斑斑的戴维在巨人之间
I felt this pee-stained
David among Goliaths

1014
00:59:51,800 --> 00:59:54,900
居然还能冲到终点，而且表现还不错。
was actually going to finish,
and finish well.

1015
00:59:57,467 --> 01:00:01,967
它想冲到终点，我就在旁边死命指挥。
It wants to make
the finishing line.
I'm just willing it on.

1016
01:00:07,067 --> 01:00:08,267
到了！
It's there!

1017
01:00:13,000 --> 01:00:14,867
[欢呼] 是啊！
[CHEERING] Yes!

1018
01:00:18,467 --> 01:00:21,300
你这台超棒的小车！
You brilliant little car!

1019
01:00:21,333 --> 01:00:23,567
天呐，简直太给力了。
God, this is just brilliant.

1020
01:00:26,233 --> 01:00:28,100
简直史诗级的。
It's absolutely epic.

1021
01:00:33,167 --> 01:00:35,567
[播报员含糊不清地说话]
[ANNOUNCER
SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]

1022
01:00:38,500 --> 01:00:40,500
[掌声]
[APPLAUSE]

1023
01:00:46,500 --> 01:00:48,400
我能说句话吗？- 什么？
Can I just say?
- What?

1024
01:00:48,433 --> 01:00:54,733
那……那是我们干过最难的事——整整二十四小时保持好人。
That was... that was the hardest thing
we've ever done. Being nice for 24 hours.

1025
01:00:54,767 --> 01:00:57,367
哦，我知道。当我把车开出维修区，你说“祝好运，兄弟”，
Ooh, I know. You know when I pulled out
the pits and you said "Good luck, mate",

1026
01:00:57,400 --> 01:01:00,700
我差点撞车！- 哦，我说这话感觉自己好像脏了，真不对劲。
I nearly crashed!
- Oh, and I felt dirty saying it mate,
it was wrong.

1027
01:01:01,000 --> 01:01:05,100
不过我们最后在本组拿了第三。- 五辆里。
Still, we ended up coming 3rd in our class.
- Out of 5.

1028
01:01:05,133 --> 01:01:11,533
对，五辆里排第三，整体上我们在46辆中排第39，部分原因是你的驾驶。
Out of 5, yes, and we finished 39th out
of 46, partly because of your driving.

1029
01:01:11,900 --> 01:01:14,300
哦，先别急——
Oh, now come on a minute-
- Actually, hang on, you wished us

1030
01:01:14,333 --> 01:01:17,467
其实等等，你刚才祝我们根本别想完赛，因为你最后一段开得像个傻瓜。
not finishing at all, by driving
like an idiot in that last stint.

1031
01:01:17,500 --> 01:01:20,100
不对，如果你没撞那辆 Mosler，我们肯定会第十名，
No, but we would have finished
10th, mathematical certainty,

1032
01:01:20,133 --> 01:01:22,967
绝对有把握！
if you hadn't hit that Mosler.
We would've been 10th!

1033
01:01:23,000 --> 01:01:26,367
你说不是我的错！- 我当时是好意说的，真不是想讽刺！
You said it wasn't my fault!
- I was being nice, I didn't mean it!

1034
01:01:27,000 --> 01:01:29,967
嘿，这才像话吧？正常服务已经恢复了。
Hey, this is more like it, isn't it?
Normal service has been resumed.

1035
01:01:30,000 --> 01:01:34,900
是啊，而且会在下周继续——哦不，因为台球赛所以下周不行。
It has, yes, and it will continue next week
oh no, not next week because of snooker.

1036
01:01:35,500 --> 01:01:40,867
不过两周后我们会带着《Top Gear》大奖回归。到时见，晚安！
But we'll be back in two weeks with the
Top Gear Awards. See you then, goodnight!

1037
01:01:40,900 --> 01:01:45,900
